I love getting bones piles. They tend to make one's game much easier,
with the large amount of food, money, stuff, and decent armor and
weapons in them.

I was having a great wizard game the other day. Started with a ring of
invisibility. Found large wand shop on level 2 with a wand of death
among other things. (When I realized the wand was worth 500 gp, my
heart was jumping for a while because there was a decent chance that
it would be a WOW.) Found magic lamp early on. Found speed boots and
other neat stuff in an armor shop on level 4. (There were *6* shops
and 7 altars in the game.)

The only problem is that I didn't want to be playing a wizard. If you
start with the right stuff they are way too easy, and since my best
wizard score has nine figures, I wasn't going to beat that unless I
played a really long time. Also, some previous player had left
Excalibur in a bones pile, so I wasn't going to be able to make myself
a nice +20 weapon.

It's always been my dream to find a super bones pile, like from
someone who has just raided the castle. Unfortunately, such bones
piles are always way down in the dungeon and by the time I get there I
already have the stuff I need. I've often been tempted to *make* such
a pile by intentionally killing one of my awesome characters on level
4, and then pick up the bones pile with a new wimpy character. However
the 1/3 chance always has made me turn this option down and go on to
try for demigodhood.

This time however, I decided to try it! (On level 5 instead because
there was a shop on level 4, and I wasn't 100% sure that a bones level
would be generated on a shop level.) Anyway, I started up a couple of
characters (in a difficult character class of course), and ran them
down to the downstair on level 4. (I wanted to make sure to pick up
any pile right away and not have anybody else happen to come across
it.) Anyway, to make a long story short, I zapped my wizard with his
wand of death (after dropping everything else of course), and.......
It left a bones level!

So, I had a wimpy level 3 knight, who in a bones pile found...

  Gray dragon scale mail, speed boots, shield of reflection, gauntlets of dex,
    cloak of displacement, and a Hawaiian shirt (Lowest enchantment on any of
    these was +5.)
  A +8 Mjollnir, Fire and Frost brand for resistances, another artifact, and
    a blessed athame.
  Useful wands including, a wand of death, 2 poly wands, cancellation,
    make invisible, teleportation, speed monster, and the completely unused
    Wand of Wishing from the castle!
  Potions of holy water along with a blessed gain ability potion.
  3 blessed scrolls of charging.
  Useful tools such as a blindfold, magic marker, unicorn horn, skeleton key,
    and pick-axe.
  Other useful stuff including gauntlets of power, helm of opposite alignment,
    rings of invisibility and regeneration, blessed luckstone, not to mention
    5 figures worth of gold and lots of food.

Another reason I chose level 5 instead of level 4 was that there was a
floating eye on level 5. My knight promptly killed it and it even left
a corpse! This is going to be an easy game :) I could probably finish
it in a relatively small number of moves and with a very low score,
for those who value those types of games. Of course, this is YARNA
(Yet Another Absolutely Ridiculous Nethack Abuse), but still,
sometimes you just got to go for that 1 in 3 chance and see what you
can come up with ;)

